
1. Examine the file redis:
It is of the form:
IP=192.x.y.z
PORT=6379

The IP is the addtess of a Redis server, and thePORT is the default connection port.

Run:
     ./toAtlast.py redis test.atl

And you will get the message:

    Successfully converted redis to test.atl using base name 'redis'

Now run the test command:
    
    atlast -v -I redisTest.atl

If it succeeds then would see this (or something very similar).:

ATLAST 1.2++ (2007-10-07) This program is in the public domain.
Compiled: Aug  6 2026 14:08:02

Verbose True

ATL_PATH = /usr/local/lib/atlast/
Loading ... start.atl
Loading ... redisTest.atl
Initialising redis connection.
Stack: Empty.->

At this point the test is complete.

